      "note": "Uploader tag disputed by model output, cross-validated but still unverified by ear. Essentia's voice/instrumental classifier reads this as vocal with high confidence, independently, in two separate runs: a Node.js harness (mean p(voice) 0.88, max 1.00, 100% of sampled segments over threshold) and a live browser run driving the real capture pipeline through Playwright/Chromium with genuine getUserMedia audio (vocalPresence 0.5-1.0 across the listening window, mood_party 0.93 — the highest of any track in the set). Same model, same weights, two independently-built pipelines (different resampling/windowing code paths) agreeing is stronger evidence than either run alone, but it is still model output, not a human ear. House/club tracks commonly carry vocal hooks, and Jamendo's tags are uploader-supplied rather than expert annotation. Left as-is deliberately: treat this track as unlabelled rather than as either a confirmed model error or a confirmed tag error — the cross-validation raises confidence that the model is picking up something real, not that the uploader's tag is wrong."
